  ],
  "notes": "More literary and formal than {危|あぶ}ない. The adjective form {危|あや}うい is used predicatively to describe precarious situations. The adverbial form {危|あや}うく is extremely common in the pattern {危|あや}うく～ところだった (I almost ~).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {命|いのち}が{危|あや}うい — one's life is in danger\n- {立場|たちば}が{危|あや}うい — one's position is precarious\n- {危|あや}うく～ところだった — almost did ~\n- {危|あや}うく{難|なん}を{逃|のが}れる — to narrowly escape danger",
